# BDD Testing

Purpose:
  BDD Testing

Skill: BDD Testing

ID:
  SKILL-CROSS-TEST-BDD

Domain:
  cross-cutting/testing

Use:
  behavior-driven testing

Apply:
  intermediate
  senior
  acceptance-testing
  collaboration

Requires:
  testing-fundamentals
  cucumber-or-gherkin

Avoid:
  vague-scenarios
  implementation-details
  over-specification
  test-pollution

Level:
  L2

Status:
  STABLE

Maturity:
  MATURE

Risk:
  LOW

Review:
  2026-08

Version:
  1.0

EvidenceLevel:
  HIGH

SearchKeys:
  bdd
  cucumber
  gherkin
  behavior-driven
  acceptance test
  scenario

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/cross-cutting/testing/bdd.md

Evidence:
  - Cucumber Documentation
  - BDD Methodology
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [B1] Scenarios MUST describe behavior, not implementation.
  [B2] Use Given-When-Then format.
  [B3] Scenarios MUST be independent.
  [B4] Use domain language in scenarios.
  [B5] One scenario per behavior.
  [B6] Include edge cases and error scenarios.
  [B7] Automate scenarios that are run frequently.
  [B8] Review scenarios with product owners.

Pros:
  - Shared understanding
  - Living documentation
  - Reduced rework

Cons:
  - Writing good scenarios is hard
  - Maintenance overhead

Alternatives:
  - TDD
  - ATDD
  - Property-based testing

State: +

